BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 352 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 337 Td (Welcome to The First-Time Manager. The biggest change in your first year is not a new) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 322 Td (title, it is a new job. You used to be measured on your own work. Now you are measured) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 307 Td (on what your team achieves. That shift is mostly about where you spend your attention.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 292 Td (Many new managers keep doing the work they were good at, because it feels safe, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 277 Td (then have no time left to lead. In this lecture we cover one to ones, delegation and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 262 Td (feedback, which are the three habits that make the first year work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 247 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 0.094 0.094 0.106 rg 56 226 Td (What to let go of first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 206 Td (- Tasks others can learn to do) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 191 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 176 Td (- The need to be the expert) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 161 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 146 Td (- Being available for everything) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 131 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 116 Td (Letting go is hard because the tasks you drop are often the ones you do best. Start) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 101 Td (with work that someone else can learn, even if they will do it slower at first. Let go) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 86 Td (of needing to be the expert in the room, because your value now is helping others do) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 71 Td (well. And let go of being available for every question, since constant interruptions) Tj ET
